    "qualification": "retain the current non-dominated conservative default; no universal optimum is established",
    "rationale": [
      "The current policy is on the eleven-policy Pareto frontier and has no dominator across mean exposure, worst exposure, maximum byte gap, minimum last-preview PSNR, and mean generation count.",
      "It ranks fifth of 56 for mean byte-weighted exposure MSE, third for worst exposure, and first for minimum last-preview PSNR.",
      "Alternative leaders optimize mutually conflicting pixel-domain objectives and have not been tested under network timing, UI presentation, energy, or subjective tasks."
    ],
    "supportedClaims": [
      "On the fixed macOS/ImageIO environment and retained corpus, all 104 scan entropy prefixes are rasterizable before the terminating marker arrives.",
      "Fresh and repeatedly updated incremental sources produce identical pixels at all 388 recorded checkpoints.",
      "CGImageSource frame status is not a sufficient preview-availability oracle in this experiment because rasterizable fresh prefixes report an incomplete status.",
      "The current 1/2/4/8 policy is non-dominated within the explicitly enumerated 56-policy, four-threshold candidate set under the stated pixel-domain objectives."
    ],
    "unsupportedClaims": [
      "The current policy is optimal for arbitrary JPEG scan scripts, image distributions, operating systems, devices, networks, or user tasks.",
      "Entropy-end rasterizability is an Apple framework contract across OS releases.",
      "Byte-weighted MSE or PSNR is a sufficient proxy for perceived usefulness, recognition, jank, or energy.",
      "The experiment justifies increasing preview count or changing public generation semantics."
    ]
  },
